==============================================================================
WHAT THIS REPORT EVIDENCES
==============================================================================

  Twelve testcases across the complaint event listener surface: assignee
  change; participant added and participant deleted; priority change; location
  update, including the case where the previous location was empty; status
  change; calendar folder deletion; details change, including the case where
  the previous details were null; and two guard cases, a null event and a
  source that is not a complaint.  At twelve of this module's twenty seven unit
  testcases this is the largest single report in the directory.  The next
  largest holds three.

  The class drives its collaborators through the mocking library's static API
  and touches the calendar, outlook, object history and participants domain
  types together with an exchange service delete mode enumeration.  That
  mocking library advances from 4.1 to 5.6.0.  Both 4.1 and the intermediate
  4.3 fail identically on Java 17 with an inaccessible object error raised from
  the library's own class proxy factory, and the resolution was to advance the
  library rather than to relax a JDK module boundary.  Seven of this module's
  eight unit test classes use that library, and the advance reaches all of them
  purely through the version property in the root aggregator.  This module's
  own build file is consequently not edited at all: it names the library as a
  test dependency and declares no version for it, nor for any other test
  library.

  Because this class exercises the widest behavioural surface in the module, a
  difference between this report and its baseline twin would be the most
  informative single signal in the directory.  There is no such difference to
  report.  Both sides record twelve tests with no failure, no error and no
  skip, the same twelve names and the same execution order, and the only
  material difference between them is the recorded runtime.  Should this report
  ever record a failure or an error, that entry owes a row in the baseline test
  failure register, and a failure with no matching row there is a migration
  regression rather than an accepted baseline condition.

  THE LIMIT OF THIS EVIDENCE: this is a unit report.  The spreadsheet driven
  numbering and routing behaviour that this module participates in is proven by
  the smoke flows and not here.  Two of the eight captured flows bear directly
  on this module, the object numbering flow and the queue transition flow, and
  they are corroborating context, each judged on its own record.  Coverage
  liveness is evidenced by
  docs/migration/smoke-evidence/migrated/jacoco-liveness.txt and this report
  must be read together with it, because a green run whose instrumentation has
  been severed measures nothing at all while still exiting zero.

