NOT BYTE COMPARABLE
==============================================================================

  Unlike the five frontend build artefacts, which are judged by byte identity,
  this archive is not judged that way.  A runner report carries an elapsed time
  for the suite and for every testcase, and a record of the runtime it ran on.
  Where a class writes to the console the report carries that payload too,
  stamped with wall clock times and thread names by this module's own test
  logging configuration, whose console appender writes to standard output under
  a pattern that begins with a timestamp.  This particular class emits nothing
  at the configured level, so no console payload is present, but the elapsed
  times alone differ between any two runs by construction.

  Compare the two sides on testcase presence, on outcome, and on the content of
  any failure message.  Never on raw bytes.  Archived in its entirety governs
  content completeness, not byte identity.  For this class the runtime record
  is itself the comparison worth naming: the twin records a class file version
  of 52.0 and this side records 61.0, which is the whole migration expressed in
  a single attribute.

